Approach: Use sliding window of size k. Compute initial sum, then slide the window by removing left element and adding next right element while tracking maximum sum.

Time Complexity: O(n) — each element is added and removed once.

Space Complexity: O(1) — no extra space used apart from variables.

class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        int left=0,right=k-1;
        double sum=0,maxsum=0;
        for(int i=left;i<=right;i++){
              sum+=nums[i];
        }
        maxsum=sum;
        while(right<nums.length-1){
            sum-=nums[left];
            left++;
            right++;
            sum+=nums[right];
            maxsum=Math.max(maxsum,sum);
        }
        return maxsum/k;
    }
}
